{"packet_id":"D067-03","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Anti-Eviction Act statutory grounds for eviction","requirement":"A landlord may evict only for the statutory grounds in the Anti-Eviction Act, with a Notice to Quit ranging from three days to 18 months (three years for conversion). Illegal-occupancy evictions require relocation assistance of six times the monthly rent.","key_value":"6 times monthly rent","coverage_conditions":"Most residential rentals: single-family homes, mobile homes and mobile home park land, apartment buildings and complexes, and rooming and boarding homes.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Exceptions turn on owner-occupancy of two- or three-unit premises"},"exemptions":"May not apply to two- or three-unit owner-occupied premises with two or fewer rental units; hotel, motel or guest-house transient or seasonal guests; a unit held in trust for a permanently occupying immediate family member who is developmentally disabled.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"Any tenant evicted under G 3) (illegal occupancy) is entitled to relocation assistance in an amount equal to six times the tenant’s monthly rent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-03","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Self-help eviction and lockout prohibition","requirement":"A landlord may not padlock, disconnect utilities or otherwise block entry, and may not remove a tenant without a court order; self-help evictions and lockouts are illegal, and only a court officer may physically evict after a warrant for removal.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental dwellings in New Jersey; applies to landlords and anyone acting on the landlord's behalf.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All rental dwellings in New Jersey"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"A person who illegally evicts may be liable for damages, including court costs and reasonable attorney fees, and may be charged with disorderly conduct.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:39-1","quoted_span":"A landlord or their agent may not padlock, disconnect utilities or otherwise block entry to a rental premise while the tenant still lives there.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-03","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Anti-Eviction Act unconscionable rent increase limit","requirement":"A rent increase must not be unconscionable and must comply with all other laws and municipal ordinances, including rent control; a tenant may withhold the difference while the court decides whether the increase is unconscionable.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies covered by the Anti-Eviction Act that receive a notice of rent increase.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":null},"exemptions":"Same Anti-Eviction Act exceptions: two- or three-unit owner-occupied premises with two or fewer rental units; transient hotel or motel guests.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"The rent increase must not be unconscionable and must comply with all other laws or municipal ordinances, including rent control.","interaction":"Rent increases must comply with municipal rent control ordinances.","confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
